.TH XHIDECURSOR 1 "" "xhidecursor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xhidecursor \- hide the mouse cursor when typing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xhidecursor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xhidecursor
hides the mouse cursor on key presses and shows it again on mouse movement. Modifier keys are ignored.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
XInput2 >= 2.1 and XFixes >= 4.0 are required.
.SH AUTHOR
Aleksandrs Stier <aleks.stier@icloud.com>.
